WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.137
The rule with Intune is simple:
Intune owns device certificates,

2
00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.450
and the platform stays out of its way.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.879
If some Intune certificates still come
from AD CS during the transition,

4
00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:14.938
the platform will see them, and it
just watches — it doesn't renew them.

5
00:00:14.938 --> 00:00:19.558
CyberArk can also act as Intune's certificate
authority, but the program says no,

6
00:00:19.558 --> 00:00:24.038
because that would create a second issuer
for devices that are mid-migration.

7
00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:28.004
And there's no built-in way to
pull in Cloud PKI's inventory;

8
00:00:28.004 --> 00:00:32.540
it would take a custom job, so
Intune's own report stays the record.
